Package: DrWrinch
Title: Fully Specified Bayes Factors for Process Tracing
Version: 0.0.1.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matias", "Lopez", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           email = "matiaslopez.uy@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0871-2841")),
    person("Jake", "Bowers", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "jwbowers@illinois.edu",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4048-1166")),
    person("Daniel", "Gajardo Cooper", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           email = "drgajardo@uc.cl"))
Description: Computes fully specified Bayes factors for process tracing,
    as developed in Lopez, Bowers, and Gajardo Cooper (2026). The package
    implements two generative models for evidence in favor of a working
    theory against a single rival: a binomial model for open-ended
    evidence collection, and a hypergeometric urn model for bounded
    archives. Both models yield Bayes factors that tilt in favor of the
    rival theory by construction, so the reported Bayes factor is a
    lower bound on the evidence for the working theory. Sensitivity
    analyses vary coding error and observation bias to show how the
    conclusion changes under departures from the baseline assumptions.
    Named after Dorothy Maud Wrinch (1894--1976,
    <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorothy_Maud_Wrinch>), whose joint
    papers with Harold Jeffreys (1919, 1921, 1923) developed the
    framework that became Jeffreys's theory of Bayes factors.
